        "original_id": "bd3fbcd1-b249-58d2-826c-612f7d8e5ee0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Arthur Koestler, Carl Jung, Eugen Bleuler\n- Books: The Roots of Coincidence\n- Concepts: parapsychology, extrasensory perception, psychokinesis, synchronicity, analytical psychology\n- Places: Burghölzli hospital\n\nFacts:\n- In 1972, Arthur Koestler published the bestselling book The Roots of Coincidence.\n- The Roots of Coincidence is an introduction to theories of parapsychology, including extrasensory perception and psychokinesis.\n- The Roots of Coincidence was influenced by Carl Jung's concept of synchronicity.\n- Carl Jung was a Swiss psychiatrist and psychoanalyst who founded analytical psychology.\n- Carl Jung worked as a notable research scientist at Burghölzli hospital under Eugen Bleuler.",
